{"id": "e3e70791-9570-4c3b-8e38-2d2f18a77aae", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T10:32:47.824637", "source": "agent", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "The lexer has an issue \u2014 the `ws` variable is defined but never used, and the whitespace skip rule is calling `token` recursively with the wrong argument. Let me fix the lexer:\n\n"}], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"thought": "The FsLex error says \"The macro ws is not defined\". Looking at the lexer, the issue is that `ws` is defined as a pattern but then referenced in the rule body as `token (lexeme lexbuf)`. The `ws` variable in the pattern `whitespace+ as ws` is bound but the body doesn't use it \u2014 that's fine for F# but FsLex might be treating it differently.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the issue is that in FsLex, the `as ws` binding creates a variable, but the body `{ token (lexeme lexbuf) }` doesn't reference `ws`. The error \"The macro ws is not defined\" suggests FsLex is checking that all `as` bindings are used in the action. Let me remove the unused `as ws` binding.\n", "kind": "ThinkAction"}, "tool_name": "think", "tool_call_id": "17b4b3d8-630e-4aa0-a9db-362f1a0b25db", "tool_call": {"id": "17b4b3d8-630e-4aa0-a9db-362f1a0b25db", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "think", "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"The FsLex error says \\\"The macro ws is not defined\\\". Looking at the lexer, the issue is that `ws` is defined as a pattern but then referenced in the rule body as `token (lexeme lexbuf)`. The `ws` variable in the pattern `whitespace+ as ws` is bound but the body doesn't use it \\u2014 that's fine for F# but FsLex might be treating it differently.\\n\\nActually, looking more carefully, the issue is that in FsLex, the `as ws` binding creates a variable, but the body `{ token (lexeme lexbuf) }` doesn't reference `ws`. The error \\\"The macro ws is not defined\\\" suggests FsLex is checking that all `as` bindings are used in the action. Let me remove the unused `as ws` binding.\\n\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-fb0f0b25-c5e1-4193-805e-7b153734a333", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "think: {\"thought\": \"The FsLex error says \\\"The macro ws is not defined\\\". Looking at the lexer, the issue is that `ws` is defined as a pattern but then referenced in the rule body as `token (lexeme lexbuf)`. The `ws` variable in the pattern `whitespace+ as ws` is bound but the body doesn't use it \\u2014 that's fine for F# but FsLex might be treating it differently.\\n\\nActually, looking more carefully, the issue is that in FsLex, the `as ws` binding creates a variable, but the body `{ token (lexeme lexbuf) }` doesn't reference `ws`. The error \\\"The macro ws is not defined\\\" suggests FsLex is checking that all `as` bindings are used in the action. Let me remove the unused `as ws` binding.\\n\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
