{"id": "4a7b36f1-7d8d-4e6d-8d38-dfa3d261c2c1", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T10:41:31.293137", "source": "agent", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"thought": "Now I see the issue clearly. The FsYacc lexer only recognizes:\n- IDENT (identifier)\n- BAR (`|`)\n- COLON (`:`)\n- And a catch-all `unexpected_char` for anything else\n\nThe `=` character is NOT recognized. This means FsYacc 11.3.0 doesn't support the `name = production_item` syntax for binding names in grammar rules.\n\nLooking at the lexer rules:\n- Rule 17: IDENT (lexeme lexbuf) - for identifiers\n- Rule 18: BAR (`|`)\n- Rule 21: COLON (`:`)\n- Rule 22: unexpected_char - for anything else (including `=`)\n\nSo I need to use a different syntax. In classic F# FsYacc, the syntax for binding names in semantic actions is:\n- `production_item as name`\n\nLet me check the parser grammar to confirm this.\n", "kind": "ThinkAction"}, "tool_name": "think", "tool_call_id": "cf6819d0-7864-459b-a62d-add023966417", "tool_call": {"id": "cf6819d0-7864-459b-a62d-add023966417", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "think", "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"Now I see the issue clearly. The FsYacc lexer only recognizes:\\n- IDENT (identifier)\\n- BAR (`|`)\\n- COLON (`:`)\\n- And a catch-all `unexpected_char` for anything else\\n\\nThe `=` character is NOT recognized. This means FsYacc 11.3.0 doesn't support the `name = production_item` syntax for binding names in grammar rules.\\n\\nLooking at the lexer rules:\\n- Rule 17: IDENT (lexeme lexbuf) - for identifiers\\n- Rule 18: BAR (`|`)\\n- Rule 21: COLON (`:`)\\n- Rule 22: unexpected_char - for anything else (including `=`)\\n\\nSo I need to use a different syntax. In classic F# FsYacc, the syntax for binding names in semantic actions is:\\n- `production_item as name`\\n\\nLet me check the parser grammar to confirm this.\\n\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-33aba6ba-686f-47ee-9979-8d0e5fdbb551", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "think: {\"thought\": \"Now I see the issue clearly. The FsYacc lexer only recognizes:\\n- IDENT (identifier)\\n- BAR (`|`)\\n- COLON (`:`)\\n- And a catch-all `unexpected_char` for anything else\\n\\nThe `=` character is NOT recognized. This means FsYacc 11.3.0 doesn't support the `name = production_item` syntax for binding names in grammar rules.\\n\\nLooking at the lexer rules:\\n- Rule 17: IDENT (lexeme lexbuf) - for identifiers\\n- Rule 18: BAR (`|`)\\n- Rule 21: COLON (`:`)\\n- Rule 22: unexpected_char - for anything else (including `=`)\\n\\nSo I need to use a different syntax. In classic F# FsYacc, the syntax for binding names in semantic actions is:\\n- `production_item as name`\\n\\nLet me check the parser grammar to confirm this.\\n\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
